t the Ace of Diamonds on the river completes any flush draw, and my opponent has been calling consistently (suggesting a strong draw or made hand), checking is the safest option. Three Jacks is strong, but loses to any flush. With a 4-diamond board, the probability my opponent has a flush is significant. Since I'm already ahead in cumulative chips and this is late in the game, I should avoid a costly mistake. Checking allows me to see showdown without investing more chips into what could be a losing hand against a flush.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
